pydebuprep (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Configuration file /etc/pydebuprep.conf (YAML) with per-check options,
    plus configtest and example-config commands and --check-option.
  * New output formats: jira and confluence (wiki markup).
  * disk-space checks local filesystems only unless include_remote is set.
  * Snapshots record enabled as well as active services.
  * Output directory is validated before checks run; baseline host and
    release mismatches are warned about even when os-release is skipped.
  * bash and zsh completion, generated from the command-line parser and
    installed for both shells.
  * apt-mark now runs with the same read-only options as apt; as root it
    could rebuild /var/cache/apt/pkgcache.bin.
  * Regular-expression options keep commas; '-o -' writes to standard
    output even when the configuration sets output_dir; stricter config
    validation.
  * Jira/Confluence escaping covers list, strikethrough and icon markup.
  * Relative paths in the configuration file resolve against its directory.
  * Every release is built once and audited with strace on Debian 12, 13
    and Ubuntu 22.04, 24.04 and 26.04 to prove a run changes nothing.

 -- Jostein Elvaker Haande <jehaande@gmail.com>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 07:20:50 +0100

